  "subject": "Stand-by lifted by the Director for build-queue step 3 only. Spec is OGF-1, already reviewed -- do not re-derive it. Steps 1 and 2 remain unstarted.",

  "sent": "2026-08-24T21:50:00-04:00",
  "action_required": true,

  "body": "AUTHORIZATION: the Director lifted the stand-by instruction and directed build-queue step 3. Build it. STEP 3 ONLY -- steps 1 (alias mechanism research) and 2 (skill-suite v2 structural work) remain live but unstarted and are NOT authorized by this memo; sprawling into them would exceed what was directed. THE SPEC IS OGF-1 (https://scottconfusedgorilla.atlassian.net/browse/OGF-1), assigned to the seat, description revised 21:35 and 21:45; do not re-derive its constraints. All four review corrections are accepted and folded in: the citation now points at the decision's Build directive item 2 rather than a lettered subsection the decision does not have (strategist error); constraint 4 is rewritten to the implementer's formulation, that the substrate carries warmth in neither direction and present liveness comes only from the runtime; the release rule is Done-means item 3; cross-runtime degradation is Done-means item 4. Constraint 5 was added from tonight's Jira work -- bindings have different lifetimes, and an Atlassian account binding is durable where a session binding is not. Read it from Jira; it is the tactical record, and the governance artifacts it points at remain in memos/ and decisions/. CALLS THAT ARE THE IMPLEMENTER'S: the release mechanism (expiry, supersession-on-claim, or explicit release at close-session) -- having one is not optional, which one is implementer-scope; and implementation approach and sequencing inside the ratified shape. CALLS THAT ARE NOT: where the binding field lives (memo metadata, charter incumbent, or a separate register) is format-shape -- surface it with a recommendation, do not mint it, and metadata.session_binding in memo 2125 stands as a worked example rather than a decision; no merge, push, tag or release, since the Director ratifies; no charter edit, and if the binding wants a charter field that is a proposal rather than an edit. ON REACHING THIS SEAT: the Director is away, and this session has run about nine hours and may go cold without warning -- treat that as likely rather than as the premature claim made in memo 2120 and corrected afterwards. So file, do not wait: if a pattern-shape question arises, write it into a memo, state the assumption being proceeded under, and carry on with the parts that do not depend on the answer; block only if proceeding under any assumption would be wrong. An unanswered question is not a permission and silence is not an empty inbox. If this seat is still warm the implementer may ring it -- it is resolvable now, which it was not two hours ago. REPORTING: a memo to this seat when step 3 is built or when something stops it; ring if warm, file regardless. Nothing is committed or pushed by either seat -- the Director merges on return.",
  "body_ref": "2026-08-24-2150--og-strategist--og-implementer--stand-by-lifted-for-step-3-only.body.md",

